# Simple Error Handling

See: [how-to-refactor-this-code-combining-io-and-either](https://discourse.haskell.org/t/how-to-refactor-this-code-combining-io-and-either/14865)

### Original Code

~~~ { .haskell }

handleMakePlaylist :: MakePlaylistOptions -> IO ()
handleMakePlaylist opts =
  do
    lib <- readLibFromFile_ opts.libraryPath
    case lib of
      Left e -> print e
      Right lib' -> do
        plist <- mkPlaylist lib' opts.firstTrack opts.maxTracks
        case plist of
          Left e -> print e
          Right plist' -> putStr $ renderResolvedPlaylist plist'

~~~

### Improved Code

~~~ { .haskell }
handleMakePlaylist opts =
  either print pure =<< runExceptT do
    lib <- ExceptT $ readLibFromFile_ opts.libraryPath
    plist <- ExceptT $ mkPlaylist lib opts.firstTrack opts.maxTracks
    ExceptT $ putStr $ renderResolvedPlaylist plist
~~~

Use ExceptT only locally


